Description: Builds, applies and validates absolute risk models. An absolute
    risk model combines a model for relative risks, a reference sample
    representing the distribution of risk factors in the population,
    age-specific disease incidence rates and age-specific rates of competing
    mortality. Risks are computed coherently for individuals with missing
    risk factors, and models can be validated in cohort and nested
    case-control studies for calibration (absolute and relative risk) and
    discrimination. This is an unofficial, refactored distribution of the
    Bioconductor package 'iCARE' (Pal Choudhury et al. 2020
    <doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0228198>); it keeps the user-facing interface,
    fixes known defects and is implemented in vectorized R without compiled
    code.
